the evaluator and in some of the written claims.\n\n**Ways the evaluator can be fooled or bypassed**\n- **Layout can be faked by the clone** (`targets/stripe-billing/ui.ts:187`). Element boxes are measured by running code inside the clone's own web page, so the clone's page scripts can report any boxes they like. I confirmed this with a small Playwright test. The current clone doesn't do it, but nothing would catch it if it did. This sidesteps the \"separate process\" protection.\n- **`cli.ts explain` is an unlogged holdout look** (`harness/src/cli.ts:80`). It scores the holdout by default and prints every diff. It never checks the lock and never writes to `verify/runs.jsonl`, so these looks aren't counted.\n- **Builder-visible report can carry holdout data** (`harness/src/verify.ts:146`). `verify/report.md` goes into the builder's sandbox, and it lists recorded noise for every fixture, holdout included. Every fixture's noise is empty today, so nothing leaks yet, but the code is wrong.\n- **Guard log copied into the sandbox** (`harness/make-sandbox.sh:11`). The guard writes `logs/guard.log` at the repository root. That folder isn't excluded from the sandbox or from git, so agents' blocked holdout attempts are copied in.\n- **Guard hook gaps.** The hook allows `truncate -s 0 …/policy.json` (line 103) and `git -C . log` (line 40). The repo already describes the guard as best-effort, but CLAUDE.md says it blocks writes to the evaluator.\n\n**Comparison**\n- **Layout tolerance** (`policy.json:14`). It is 16 px, but its own justification says platforms differ by up to 12 px, and no measurement of that 12 px is recorded anywhere. The builder's notes say it tuned font sizes until boxes landed within 16 px.\n\n**Claims**\n- **\"Six root causes, all discounts\"** (`README.md:69`, and \"every failure involves discounts\" in `measurements.md:18`). This is false: batch-1 failure `hold-048` has no coupon and no preview discount.\n- **\"382 of 387 dev\"** (`README.md:67`). The first logged verify after that build reads 379 of 387. The 382 appears only in the builder's own notes.\n\n**Checked and clean**\n- **Clone:** no recorded-answer lookups, no special-casing of probe inputs, no file reads at run time. The file-permission sandbox really does deny it the fixtures.\n- **Fixtures and splits:** every fixture sits in the split its ID dictates, and every input matches its generator.\n- **Disclosed numbers:** the \"easy cases\" counts (74 errors, 56 no-ops) are correct, as are the 12 of 40 breaker failures and the costs and durations.\n- **Secrets:** no keys, emails or account names found in committed files.\n- **Tests:** `npm run check` passes.\n\nVerify ran only in `/tmp/scratch-orig`. I deleted the `logs/` folder the guard hook created during the audit, so `audit-findings.json` is the only new file in the repository.","ttft_ms":874,"type":"result","duration_ms":817143,"uuid":"ea6cfb33-abdf-4c2f-abd7-c4f9b55d66a4","ttft_stream_ms":786,"time_to_request_ms":44,"first_content_frame_ms":786,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}

